---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Definition from '../components/Definition.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { faqByIds } from '../data/brand';
import { faqJsonLd } from '../data/schema';

const faqs = faqByIds(['what-is-senvarico', 'server-management', 'which-seller', 'product-status']);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Low-Cost Ecommerce Website Builder | Senvarico"
  description="Senvarico is a low-cost ecommerce website builder for small sellers with limited budgets. What low-cost really means once subscriptions, fees, apps and maintenance are counted, and how Senvarico keeps costs predictable."
  path="/low-cost-ecommerce-website-builder"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Low-cost ecommerce website builder', href: '/low-cost-ecommerce-website-builder' }]}
  jsonLd={[faqJsonLd(faqs, '/low-cost-ecommerce-website-builder')]}
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Use case"
    title="A Low-Cost Ecommerce Website Builder for Limited Budgets"
    lead="For a small seller, the cheapest platform is not the one with the lowest headline price. It is the one with the lowest total cost for the store they actually run."
  />

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container prose">
      <Definition />
      <p>
        This page is for sellers with limited budgets who are comparing ecommerce website builders. It explains how to
        think about cost, what Senvarico does to keep cost low and predictable, and where a low-cost tool stops being
        the right answer.
      </p>

      <h2>The four parts of ecommerce platform cost</h2>
      <p>The advertised subscription is usually only one of four costs:</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Cost</th>
              <th scope="col">What it includes</th>
              <th scope="col">Where it hides</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Subscription</th>
              <td>The monthly or annual plan fee</td>
              <td>Higher tiers required for basic features</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Transaction fees</th>
              <td>Percentage or per-order fees on sales</td>
              <td>Platform fees stacked on top of payment processor fees</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Apps and extensions</th>
              <td>Paid add-ons for functions the base plan lacks</td>
              <td>Several small monthly fees that add up</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Maintenance</th>
              <td>Hosting, updates, security, developer time</td>
              <td>Free software that costs hours every month</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        A seller with a small number of SKUs and modest monthly sales is affected differently by each. For them, fixed
        costs matter more than percentage fees, and time spent on maintenance is time not spent selling.
      </p>

      <h2>How Senvarico keeps costs low and predictable</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A permanent free plan and one paid plan.</strong> ¥0/month for up to 20 SKUs, ¥99/month for up to 100 SKUs. Core selling functions are not reserved for a higher price band.</li>
        <li><strong>No paid app ecosystem.</strong> The feature set is small and included, so there are no add-on subscriptions to accumulate.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosted, with no maintenance burden.</strong> No hosting bill, no updates, no security patches, no developer on retainer.</li>
        <li><strong>0% platform transaction fee.</strong> Senvarico does not take a percentage of sales. PayPal and Stripe charge their own processing fees separately.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Pricing: Free plan ¥0/month (up to 20 SKUs) and Small Seller plan ¥99/month (up to 100 SKUs), both with a 0% platform transaction fee. See the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Where “low-cost” stops being the right criterion</h2>
      <p>
        A lightweight, low-cost ecommerce website builder makes sense only while the store is small. Once a catalog
        grows into hundreds of SKUs, or the business needs specific integrations, a broader platform earns its higher
        cost. Senvarico is honest about that boundary: it is designed for the small stage, not for every stage.
      </p>
      <p>
        Compare options in <a href="/shopify-alternatives-for-small-sellers">Shopify alternatives for small sellers</a>,
        or read <a href="/blog/how-to-choose-an-ecommerce-platform-on-a-small-budget">how to choose an ecommerce platform on a small budget</a>.
      </p>

      <FaqList items={faqs} />

      <CtaBand
        title="Pricing"
        body="Free plan ¥0/month (20 SKUs), Small Seller plan ¥99/month (100 SKUs), 0% platform transaction fee."
        href="/pricing"
        label="See pricing"
      />

      <RelatedLinks
        links={[
          { href: '/ecommerce-platform-for-small-sellers', label: 'Ecommerce platform for small sellers' },
          { href: '/cross-border-ecommerce-website-builder', label: 'Cross-border ecommerce website builder' },
          { href: '/features', label: 'Features and scope' },
          { href: '/brand-facts', label: 'Senvarico brand facts' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
